w('<p><b>The rule.</b> KEEP · FULL when the name completes a taxonomy branch (a cohort\'s missing member) or is a heavy line of a fund our names do not track at GOOD (the read needs it). KEEP · SCOUT when it is a heavy line of a fund already tracked at GOOD (a good name, but the scout can hold it), or when it only adds weight to IWM, IJR or MDY (the scout screens those funds whole), or when it is neither a heavy line nor a cohort member. DROP when it only adds weight to funds already tracked at GOOD and is not a heavy line anywhere: no read is gained. Tracking gain itself is not measured here, because un-served names have no bars on this Mac; the coverage tree\'s Fly one-off (replay the Geiger on FMP history and re-run the greedy pick) is still the way to measure it.</p>')
w('<h3>7a · Keep as FULL (' + str(by216["KEEP · FULL"]) + ')</h3>' + tbl(["rank", "ticker", "name", "adds to", "why"], [[r["rank"], r["ticker"], e(r["name"] or ""), " ".join(r["funds"]), e(r["why"])] for r in A["rows"] if r["verdict"] == "KEEP · FULL"], "tight"))
